"Asynchronous_communication":"The tactic Asynchronous communication addresses the stimulus inter-component communication where other's availability or processing readiness cannot be guaranteed by applying the architectural modification of introducing an intermediary message queue or broker between communicating components that buffers outgoing messages and decouples the timing of message sending from message receipt to the artifact software system during the development phase of System Architecture Definition, resulting in the system response of dispatching messages to the intermediary queue and immediately resuming sender execution, while the queue buffers and forwards messages to the receiving component upon its availability.",
"Automatic_retraining_and_deployment_triggering":"The tactic Automatic retraining and deployment triggering addresses the stimulus model performance degradation or drift detection by applying the architectural modification of automated pipeline triggering model retraining and deployment based on monitoring metrics to the artifact CI/CD Pipeline during the development phase of Operation, resulting in the system response of automatically triggering model retraining and deployment based on performance metrics.",
