"Background_queue":"The tactic Background queue addresses the stimulus a non-time-critical task of the system that does not require the calling process to block and wait for immediate completion by applying the architectural modification of introducing a background queue component and dedicated worker processes that buffer submitted tasks independently of the main execution thread and process them asynchronously to the artifact software system during the development phase of System Architecture Definition, resulting in the system response of accepting the submitted task into the background queue, immediately returning control to the calling process, and independently executing the queued tasks through background workers without blocking primary operations.",
"Binary_and_ternary_weights_training":"The tactic Binary and ternary weights training addresses the stimulus arriving inference request by applying the architectural modification of training the network with a straight-through estimator and full-precision latent weights that are discretized in the forward pass to either a binary {-1, +1} or ternary {-1, 0, +1} value set to the artifact AI model during the development phase of Modeling, resulting in the system response of computing layer outputs by applying the discretized binary or ternary weight values to incoming activations, replacing floating-point multiply-accumulate operations with low-complexity integer operations, and propagating results through the network.",
