"Internal_interface_abstraction":"The tactic Internal interface abstraction addresses the stimulus interaction request from one internal component directed at another internal component's functionality by applying the architectural modification of introducing abstraction layers at internal component boundaries that expose stable interfaces while hiding concrete implementation details to the artifact software system during the development phase of Design Definition Process, resulting in the system response of routing the interaction request through the abstraction layer to the concrete implementing component and returning the result without exposing implementation internals to the calling component.",
