"Library_Encapsulation":"The tactic Library Encapsulation addresses the stimulus software component invoking external functionality by applying the architectural modification of encapsulating reusable code behind abstraction layers or interfaces as library to the artifact software system during the development phase of System Architecture Definition, resulting in the system response of routing the invocation through the abstraction layer to the underlying library implementation, isolating the calling component from library-specific details.",
"Light_communication_protocol_usage":"The tactic Light communication protocol usage addresses the stimulus communication requests in a distributed system with resource-constrained edge nodes by applying the architectural modification of implementing lightweight publish-subscribe or request-response communication protocols with reduced message overhead to the artifact communication middleware during the development phase of System Architecture Definition, resulting in the system response of transmitting data with reduced protocol overhead and network bandwidth consumption.",
"Lightweight_framework_usage":"The tactic Lightweight framework usage addresses the stimulus execution request arriving on a resource-constrained deployment target by applying the architectural modification of selecting minimal-footprint frameworks and libraries to the artifact software system during the development phase of System Architecture Definition, resulting in the system response of processing the request by loading and invoking application logic through the selected minimal-footprint framework, forwarding execution with reduced memory allocation and runtime initialization overhead.",
